From: naoki66 <naoki66@qq.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Nov 2026 13:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: pcs: airoha: extend RX calibration to E2 silicon and PON PCS

The AN7581 PCS driver skips manual RX calibration for SoC revisions >= E2,
on the assumption that E2+ silicon autocalibrates correctly. In practice
E2 silicon (PRODUCT_ID = 2) on Gemtek W1700K HW.1.1 boards leaves RX
permanently stuck on ~80% of cold boots, while HW.1.0 (PRODUCT_ID = 1) is
reliable. The manual path retries up to AIROHA_PCS_MAX_CALIBRATION_TRY
times when FreqDet fails to lock; the autocalibration path has no
equivalent retry.

The calibration gate also only matches "airoha,an7581-pcs-eth". XR1710G
routes its 10G WAN (GDM2) through the PON PCS instance
("airoha,an7581-pcs-pon") with a USXGMII copper link, so affected units
complete copper autonegotiation and then stay at NO-CARRIER with no
"Link is Up" and no DHCP, while healthy units only work because their
default SerDes tuning happens to lock. The SDK applies the same RX
calibration and CDR recovery sequence to either external SerDes, but the
Linux driver enabled both mechanisms for the ETH PCS only.

Extend manual RX calibration to both external SerDes PCS instances and
raise the PRODUCT_ID threshold to include E2 silicon for both. Enable the
existing signal-detect/CDR recovery callback for the PON PCS as well.
Optical PON line-mode calibration is untouched.

Verified on a Gemtek W1700K HW.1.1 (E2) with stable cold boots, and on an
affected XR1710G unit where carrier recovered and the link came up at
10Gbps/Full with DHCP completing after hot reboot and cold boot. Healthy
XR1710G units are unaffected because their default tuning already locks.

Link: https://github.com/naoki66/ImmortalWrt-for-Gemtek-brightspeed/issues/44
Link: https://github.com/naoki66/ImmortalWrt-for-Gemtek-brightspeed/pull/62
Co-authored-by: Gilly <gilroyscott1970@gmail.com>
Co-authored-by: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: naoki66 <naoki66@qq.com>
---
 drivers/net/pcs/airoha/pcs-airoha-common.c | 13 +++++++----
 drivers/net/pcs/airoha/pcs-an7581.c        |  4 ++--
 2 files changed, 10 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/net/pcs/airoha/pcs-airoha-common.c
+++ b/drivers/net/pcs/airoha/pcs-airoha-common.c
@@ -1578,18 +1578,20 @@
 	if (IS_ERR(priv->xfi_rst))
 		return dev_err_probe(dev, PTR_ERR(priv->xfi_rst), "failed to get xfi reset lines\n");
 
-	/* For Ethernet PCS, read the AN7581 SoC revision to check if
-	 * manual rx calibration is needed. This is only limited to
-	 * any SoC revision before E2.
+	/* For the external SerDes PCS instances, read the AN7581 SoC
+	 * revision to check if manual RX calibration is needed. This
+	 * covers the Ethernet and PON PCS used by the 10G ports, through
+	 * E2 silicon.
 	 */
-	if (device_is_compatible(dev, "airoha,an7581-pcs-eth")) {
+	if (device_is_compatible(dev, "airoha,an7581-pcs-eth") ||
+	    device_is_compatible(dev, "airoha,an7581-pcs-pon")) {
 		u32 val;
 
 		ret = regmap_read(priv->scu, AIROHA_SCU_PDIDR, &val);
 		if (ret)
 			return ret;
 
-		if (FIELD_GET(AIROHA_SCU_PRODUCT_ID, val) < 0x2)
+		if (FIELD_GET(AIROHA_SCU_PRODUCT_ID, val) < 0x3)
 			priv->manual_rx_calib = true;
 	}
 
@@ -1650,6 +1652,7 @@
 	.alloc_regmap_fields = an7581_pcs_alloc_regmap_fields,
 	.bringup = an7581_pcs_bringup,
 	.link_up = an7581_pcs_phya_link_up,
+	.rxlock_workaround = an7581_pcs_rxlock_workaround,
 	.pon_start_rx = an7581_pcs_pon_start_rx,
 	.pon_retrain_rx = an7581_pcs_pon_retrain_rx,
 	.pon_stop_rx = an7581_pcs_pon_stop_rx,
--- a/drivers/net/pcs/airoha/pcs-an7581.c
+++ b/drivers/net/pcs/airoha/pcs-an7581.c
@@ -3269,8 +3269,8 @@
 
 	an7581_pcs_cdr_reset(priv, index, interface, false);
 
-	/* Manual RX calibration is required only for SoC before E2
-	 * revision. E2+ SoC autocalibrate RX and only CDR reset is needed.
+	/* Manual RX calibration is required for SoC revisions through E2.
+	 * E3+ SoCs autocalibrate RX and only CDR reset is needed.
 	 */
 	if (!priv->manual_rx_calib)
 		return 0;
